To help you design an end-user API for 3D camera animation in TypeScript, I'll provide you with a basic structure and some examples of endpoints. You can customize this to fit your specific requirements.

1. Import necessary modules:

```typescript
import { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from 'next';
import { Camera } from '../models/Camera';
```

2. Define the `Camera` model:

```typescript
export class Camera {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  position: [number, number, number];
  rotation: [number, number, number];
  // Add more properties as needed
}
```

3. Define the API routes:

```typescript
export default (req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) => {
  if (req.method === 'GET') {
    handleGet(req, res);
  } else if (req.method === 'POST') {
    handlePost(req, res);
  } else {
    res.status(405).json({ error: 'Method not allowed' });
  }
};

async function handleGet(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  // Get all cameras
  const cameras = await Camera.find();
  res.status(200).json(cameras);
}

async function handlePost(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  // Create a new camera
  const cameraData = req.body;
  const camera = new Camera(cameraData);
  try {
    const savedCamera = await camera.save();
    res.status(201).json(savedCamera);
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Error saving camera' });
  }
}
```

4. Add more endpoints as needed, such as updating, deleting, or retrieving specific cameras.

5. Export the API module:

```typescript
module.exports = {
  handler: (req, res) => {
    // Handle the request
  },
};
```

