1. Install the Neo4j APOC Procedures library if you haven't already. You can do this by running the following command in your Neo4j browser:
```
CALL gds.procedure.install('apoc');
```
2. Create a new script file (e.g., `import_empowerid_data.cypher`) in your Neo4j browser and paste the following code:
```cypher
// Import the data from the Account table
WITH [
    { id: accountID, type: 'Account', properties: { accountID: accountID, AccountGUID: AccountGUID } }
] AS accounts
FOREACH (account IN accounts | CALL gds.node.create(account))
YIELD nodeId;

// Import the data from the Group table
WITH [
    { id: GroupID, type: 'Group', properties: { GroupID: GroupID, GroupGUID: GroupGUID } }
] AS groups
FOREACH (group IN groups | CALL gds.node.create(group))
YIELD nodeId;

// Import the data from the GroupAccount table
WITH [
    { sourceNodeId: nodeId(account), targetNodeId: nodeId(group), properties: { GroupID: GroupID, AccountID: AccountID } }
] AS relationships
FOREACH (relationship IN relationships | CALL gds.relationship.create(relationship))
YIELD relationshipId;

// Import the data from the GroupMemberGroup table
WITH [
    { sourceNodeId: nodeId(group), targetNodeId: nodeId(groupMemberGroup), properties: { GroupID: GroupID, MemberGroupID: MemberGroupID } }
] AS relationships
FOREACH (relationship IN relationships | CALL gds.relationship.create(relationship))
YIELD relationshipId;
```
