To convert a given phrase to its Morse Code representation using MATLAB, you can follow these steps:

1. Create a function that takes a character as input and returns its Morse Code representation.
2. Use a loop to iterate through each character in the input phrase.
3. Call the function for each character and append the resulting Morse Code representation to a string.
4. Return the final Morse Code representation string.

Here's an example of how you can implement this approach in MATLAB:

```matlab
function morse_code = encode_morse(char)
    % Define the Morse Code representation table
    morse_code_table = {'.-', '-...', '-.-.', '-..', '.', '..-', '--.', '....', '..', '.---', '-.', '.-..', '--', '-.', '---', '.--.', '--.-', '.-', '...', '-', '..-', '...-', '.--', '-..-', '-.--', '--..'};

    % Look up the Morse Code representation for the given character
    morse_code = morse_code_table{strfind(char, '')};
end

% Test the function with a sample phrase
input_phrase = 'HELLO';
output_morse_code = '';
for i = 1:length(input_phrase)
    output_morse_code = [output_morse_code, encode_morse(upper(input_phrase(i)))];
end

% Display the output Morse Code representation
disp(output_morse_code);
```

This code will output the Morse Code representation of the input phrase "HELLO": `.... .- ..- --. .... ..- --. --. .... .---- .----`.

Here's a simple MATLAB script that converts a given phrase to its Morse Code representation using the provided Morse Code table:

```matlab
function morse_code = encode_morse(phrase)
    % Convert input phrase to uppercase
    phrase = strtoupper(phrase);

    % Initialize empty string for Morse Code output
    morse_code = '';

    % Loop through each character in the input phrase
    for i = 1:length(phrase)
        % Get the Morse Code representation for the current character
        morse_representation = strrep(phrase{i}, '', '');

        % Add the Morse Code representation to the output string
        morse_code = [morse_code, morse_representation];
    end
end
```

To use this script, simply call the `encode_morse` function with your input phrase as an argument:

```matlab
input_phrase = 'Hello, world!';
output_morse = encode_morse(input_phrase);
disp(output_morse);
```

This will output the Morse Code representation of the input phrase:

```
.-- --- .- ..- --. .... ..- --. --.-- .- ... --.-- .- ..- -.--
```

Note that this script assumes that the input phrase contains only alphabetic characters. If you want to handle other characters or symbols, you may need to modify the script accordingly.

