Here's a simple function that maps values from 0 to 1 and has the properties you described:

```javascript
function smoothLinearMap(x) {
  const smoothFactor = 0.2; // Adjust this value for more/less smoothing
  const linearRangeStart = 0.3; // Adjust this value for where the linear range starts
  const linearRangeEnd = 0.7; // Adjust this value for where the linear range ends

  if (x <= linearRangeStart) {
    return x * smoothFactor;
  } else if (x >= linearRangeEnd) {
    return 1 - (1 - x) * smoothFactor;
  } else {
    return x;
  }
}
```

