[{"word":"chair","length":5},{"word":"curtain","length":7},{"word":"umbrella","length":8},{"word":"skyscraper","length":11}]
```

Here's an example code snippet that uses JSON to create and manipulate a list of words with their lengths:

```javascript
const words = [
  "skyscraper",
  "chair",
  "umbrella",
  "curtain"
];

// Create an empty array to store the sorted words
const sortedWords = [];

// Loop through each word and add it to the sorted list with its length
for (let i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
  const word = words[i];
  const length = word.length;
  sortedWords.push({ word, length });
}

// Sort the sorted list by length
sortedWords.sort((a, b) => a.length - b.length);

console.log(sortedWords);
```

