response:
To create a socket for chatroom, you'll need to use a library like Socket.IO or WebSocket. Here's an example using Socket.IO:

First, install Socket.IO using npm:
```bash
npm install socket.io
```
Next, create a server using Node.js and Socket.IO:
```javascript
const http = require('http');
const socketIo = require('socket.io');

const server = http.createServer();
const io = socketIo(server);

server.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server listening on port 3000');
});

io.on('connection', (socket) => {
  console.log('User connected');

  // Handle chat messages
  socket.on('chatMessage', (message) => {
    io.emit('chatMessage', message);
  });

  // Handle user disconnection
  socket.on('disconnect', () => {
    console.log('User disconnected');
  });
});
```
Now, create a client-side script using JavaScript and Socket.IO:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Chatroom</title>
  <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/socket.io/4.0.1/socket.io.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Chatroom</h1>
  <ul id="chat-messages"></ul>
  <input type="text" id="chat-input" placeholder="Type your message...">
  <button id="send-button">Send</button>

  <script>
    const socket = io();

    socket.on('chatMessage', (message) => {
      const li = document.createElement('li');
      li.textContent = message;
      document.getElementById('chat-messages').appendChild(li);
    });

